laurel 3040: LAUREL UCACHE (2998) prints its line only after the boot thread and the console exist; both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/ios26-userland.md "JIT code".

[V phone 2026-11-07 03:42] The first laurel_ucache_apply() call of 2998 is in arm_init() right after PE_init_platform(FALSE), and its
printf was the first printf of the kernel: start.s leaves TPIDR_EL1 = 0 and arm_init sets the boot thread only after
ml_parse_cpu_topology(); printf -> os_log_with_args -> counter_inc -> current_thread()->machine faults at a small address, the
exception vector reads TPIDR_EL1 again and faults again: a silent hang. The early framebuffer console showed "SWEET EARLY 1: arm_init
entered (MMU on)" and "SWEET EARLY 2: PE_init_platform done" and never "3: ml_parse_cpu_topology done"; no panic text, no USB
(logs/usblog-20261107-034407.txt stays empty). In the diff from the last kernel that booted (72a5244) that call is the only new code
between the two marks. The kill switch laurelucache=0 printed its "off" line from the same place, so it hung the same way.
Fix: the decision and the SCTLR_EL1.UCI clear stay at every call; the one line waits for the first call with startup_phase >=
STARTUP_SUB_TUNABLES (after kernel_startup_bootstrap(): the second call of arm_init, right before PE_init_platform(TRUE), whose
"iBoot version" line is the first printf of a good boot). Host test: scripts/laurel/test-ucache.sh (the guard is in front of every printf).

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/laurel_ucache.c b/osfmk/arm64/laurel_ucache.c
--- a/osfmk/arm64/laurel_ucache.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/laurel_ucache.c
